## The telegraph office

::bg{location="harl_platform" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The telegraph office is a hut with a stove, a clerk in fingerless gloves, and a pad of pink forms. Eleven words to the shilling.
@narrator{code="0020" when="visited('harl.platform')"}: The clerk looks up from the same pink pad. "Made up your mind, Inspector?"

<branch id="wire" prompt="Whom do you wire?">
  <choice id="board" label="The Medical Board at Ossery: what did Dr. Solt sign for?" into="run.wired" value="board">
    @inspector{code="0010"}: Medical Board, Ossery. Whatever you hold on an Emmerich Solt. Reply to the train.
    @narrator{code="0030"}: The key chatters. The clerk counts the words twice and charges you for three more.
  </choice>
  <choice id="varn" label="The Varn police: what do they know of Crane?" into="run.wired" value="varn">
    @inspector{code="0020"}: Varn Constabulary. Tobiah Crane, conductor. And Aurel Hask, while you are about it.
  </choice>
  <choice id="later" label="Not yet." into="run.wired" value="none">
    @inspector{code="0030" mono}: A wire is a question you only get to ask once tonight. Not until I know which.
  </choice>
</branch>
